# id: M30-leader-counts-its-own-unsynced-append
# covering-test: TestLeaderCountsItsOwnCopyOnlyWhenDurable
# package: ./raft/
# expect: killed
# power-unreachable: trace identity, 10k seeds -- unreachable on this schedule mix by construction: every node has the same modelled disk, so the leader's own fsync always lands before any follower's ack. Measured trace-identical over 10k seeds. A floor would be a floor on zero. REFUTED at DESIGN-A6 section 43.5, and RED until Ansh rules. Not merely stale in its reason -- REACHABLE AND CAUGHT. Measured at 300 seeds against a clean tree at the same 300: the clean tree is 0 of 300 with sweepfail=0; this mutation is 1 of 300, FIRST AT SEED 178, and a SAFETY VIOLATION the baseline does not have. The oracle that names it is leader completeness: 'range 1: entry index 187 term 1 was committed (first applied by node 1 at instant 7133514064) but node 1, leading in later term 2 from instant 9201825394, had persisted 0 entries above a snapshot at 186, without it' -- which is COMMITTED IS FOREVER, broken, and is exactly what this mutation plants: a leader counting toward the commit quorum a copy it has not written, then losing the unsynced write. The sentence above was true when it was measured and went STALE when A5 and A6 reshaped the schedule mix, which is A2's kill-time amendment: a schedule mix is a claim about reachability. The census at 30 seeds is also NOT identical, so the trace-identity claim does not hold either. NO OTHER DETECTOR: the argument cannot be made and must not be -- the detector cited is the strongest there is and it no longer holds. DISPOSITION, recommended and NOT taken: a rate floor derived from a single detection is noise (floors.go's own rule), so this wants 'power-detector: sweep' at 300 seeds on M73's precedent, not a rate. Turning a red lane green is the direction that needs the ruling
# power-refute-claim: census-identical
# mutates: the leader advances its own match index on append instead of on durability, so it counts a copy it has not written toward the commit quorum -- DR-8's first gate with the leader on the other end of it, where the message is elided because the leader is talking to itself
--- a/raft/raft.go
+++ b/raft/raft.go
@@ -546,11 +546,7 @@
 	}
 	e := Entry{Term: r.term, Index: r.lastIndex() + 1, ID: id, Data: append([]byte(nil), data...)}
 	r.appendEntries(e)
-	// The leader's own match index is NOT advanced here. A leader counts its own
-	// replication only once the entry is durable, and AckPersisted is where that
-	// happens; setting it on append would count a copy the leader has not
-	// written, which is the same ack-before-sync this package gates every
-	// outbound message against.
+	r.matchIndex[r.peerIdx(r.id)] = e.Index
 	r.broadcastAppend()
 	return nil
 }
